{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והגעתם אל המשקוף ואל", :translit "v'higatem el ha'mashkof v'el", :gloss "and you shall touch the lintel and"} {:he "ונתנו על שתי המזוזות ועל המשקוף", :translit "v'natnu al shtei ha'me'zuzot v'al ha'mashkof", :gloss "and they shall place [it] on the two doorposts and on the lintel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order reversal between two verses: in 12:22 mashkof precedes mezuzot; in 12:7 mezuzot precedes mashkof."}], :frame {:text "Two verses describe placing the Paschal blood on the doorposts and lintel: Exodus 12:7 writes 'on the two doorposts and on the lintel' (ונתנו על שתי המזוזות ועל המשקוף) while Exodus 12:22 writes 'the lintel and the two doorposts' (ואל שתי המזוזות — preceded by אל המשקוף). The differing orders teach that the precise sequence is not legally essential: one who changes the order still fulfills his obligation.", :sources ["Exodus 12:7" "Exodus 12:22"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מן הדם", :translit "min ha'dam", :gloss "from the blood"} {:he "דמי מילה", :translit "d'mei milah", :gloss "blood of circumcision"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מן הדם", :b "דמי מילה"}], :frame {:text "The blood of the Paschal offering is linked to the blood of circumcision. Ezekiel 16:6 says 'I passed over you and saw you wallowing in your bloods' — written in the plural (בדמיך), which is read as referring to two bloods: the blood of the Paschal lamb and the blood of circumcision (Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Pischa 7). The Exodus from Egypt was made possible by the merit of the blood of circumcision that Israel performed.", :sources ["Ezekiel 16:6" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Pischa 7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order reversal between two verses: in 12:22 mashkof precedes mezuzot; in 12:7 mezuzot precedes mashkof.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "מן הדם", :a-value 139, :b "דמי מילה", :b-value 139, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-